<title>INDIA: Indian soybean markets shut due to traders' strike.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean markets shut due to traders' strike.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean markets in central India remained closed for the seventh day on Tuesday due to an indefinite strike by traders, their leaders said.</p>
<p>Traders were protesting against the doubling of mandi (market) tax to 2.0 percent, effective May 1.</p>
<p>Some more commodities markets are expected to be closed from Wednesday in support of the striking soybean traders.</p>
<p>Bombay Commodities +91-22-265 9000</p>
